Task 1 Reflection:
The SQL INNER JOIN combined checkout records with registered member information using member_id, while the WHERE condition helped keep records with valid member IDs. The pandas merge then added book metadata from the JSON catalog using book_id, allowing each checkout to include information such as the title, author, genre, and publisher. Finally, the HTML table was extracted with BeautifulSoup and pandas, its column names were standardized, and the 26 Reading Kickoff checkout records were appended to the combined dataset. This produced a final dataset containing 417 records from all three data sources.